on points" 13194139533934 true] [17592186267027 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533934 true] [17592186267027 1111 #uuid "9bf69e79-9139-55ec-b7a7-88e4ddd26dbe" 13194139533934 true] [17592186267028 1034 "$(0,\\sqrt{3})$ and $(0,-\\sqrt{3})$" 13194139533934 true] [17592186267028 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533934 true] [17592186267028 1111 #uuid "7036a57c-e651-5337-9702-efb1a0485a1e" 13194139533934 true] [17592186267029 1017 #edb/ref 17592186267030 13194139533934 true] [17592186267029 1089 "q-79253" 13194139533934 true] [17592186267029 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533934 true] [17592186267029 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13955472/assets/32d2ecb4cc0fe71888d4ca89f0c5c493d0746ae9f97a9253ef42d69f45880086.png)\n\nWhat is the $x$-intercept of the parabola shown above?" 13194139533934 true] [17592186267029 1113 #uuid "55a39868-2114-5c28-aa42-9882eb80ca08" 13194139533934 true] [17592186267029 1145 "First, we need to find the equation of the parabola. From the diagram, we see that the parabola has a vertex at $(9,4)$ and passes through the point $(-7,12).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola with vertex $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(y-k)^{2}=4p(x-h).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $(h,k)=(9,4)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n(y-4)^{2}=4p(x-9).\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $(-7,12),$ we substitute $x=-7$ and $y=12$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(12-4)^{2} & =4p(-7-9) \\\\ 64 & =4p\\cdot (-16) \\\\ p & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-4)^{2} & =-4(x-9).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $x$-axis, we must have $y=0.$ So, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the parabola and solve the resulting equation for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0-4)^{2} & =-4(x-9) \\\\ 16 & =-4(x-9) \\\\ -4 & =x-9 \\\\ x & =-4+9 \\\\ x & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercept is $5.$" 13194139533934 true] [17592186267030 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267031 13194139533934 true] [17592186267030 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267032 13194139533934 true] [17592186267030 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267033 13194139533934 true] [17592186267030 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267034 13194139533934 true] [17592186267030 1000 #edb/ref 17592186267035 13194139533934 true] [17592186267030 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533934 true] [17592186267030 1041 "selection" 13194139533934 true] [17592186267030 1104 #edb/ref 17592186267035 13194139533934 true] [17592186267030 1110 #uuid "92de9ed0-23fb-5ce3-a28d-bbdad3bb8222" 13194139533934 true] [17592186267031 1034 "\\frac{9}{2}" 13194139533934 true] [17592186267031 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533934 true] [17592186267031 1111 #uuid "ce6dd8fc-afbf-57c9-8fab-c8122240ba64" 13194139533934 true] [17592186267032 1034 "\\frac{11}{2}" 13194139533934 true] [17592186267032 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533934 true] [17592186267032 1111 #uuid "0eb02928-44ea-5d32-8758-0669151e9f23" 13194139533934 true] [17592186267033 1034 "6" 13194139533934 true] [17592186267033 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533934 true] [17592186267033 1111 #uuid "75fbc113-a573-54ec-8e74-b8ca43f3455b" 13194139533934 true] [17592186267034 1034 "4" 13194139533934 true] [17592186267034 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533934 true] [17592186267034 1111 #uuid "69280b0f-a6e1-548b-b3d8-14fb06c58c03" 13194139533934 true] [17592186267035 1034 "5" 13194139533934 true] [17592186267035 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533934 true] [17592186267035 1111 #uuid "c4c91fb6-e219-5401-9b29-aafdd6b2514c" 13194139533934 true] [17592186267036 1017 #edb/ref 17592186267037 13194139533934 true] [17592186267036 1089 "q-79294" 13194139533934 true] [17592186267036 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533934 true] [17592186267036 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13955472/assets/407f89e40691ddaefd91